# The published OpenAPI artifact is compared byte for byte against a freshly
# built document by `server/src/v1/openapi/drift.test.ts`. `core.autocrlf` is
# `true` on the Windows checkouts this repository is developed on, which would
# otherwise hand that comparison a CRLF file to match against an LF string —
# a drift failure that is really a line-ending failure, on a fresh clone, with
# a message about the contract being stale.
#
# The check normalises line endings anyway, so this is the other half: it keeps
# the *published* document byte-stable across platforms, which matters for a
# file a docs pipeline and a client generator both consume.
docs/api/v1/openapi.json text eol=lf

# TypeScript source files must use LF line endings.  On Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true a tool that re-encodes file content (e.g. a mojibake repair
# script) can silently write CRLF or CR CR LF.  Declaring eol=lf here prevents
# git from converting these files on checkout and makes any stray CR visible.
*.ts  text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
